Patch 03 — Enable the compiled-out reverb (Phase 4, gate-proven)

Why: upstream ships the full reverb DSP (FX/Reverb.c, a Spin-Semi-style
allpass-loop design dating to the 2014 LXR-01 codebase) but compiles it out
with USE_REVERB 0 (Core/Inc/Soundengine/FxBus.h) and the {"rev"} entry
commented out of the fxNames menu table. The Phase 4 gate (see STATUS.md)
proved the DSP complete, stable and inert for existing kits — FX type is a
kit byte and no existing kit contains value 5 — so the define flips in the
copied build tree like every other patch. Removing this file restores the
exact upstream behaviour. The experiment flag route that proved it
(Makefile OPT_PATCHES) is retained for A/B builds.

--- a/Core/Inc/Soundengine/FxBus.h
+++ b/Core/Inc/Soundengine/FxBus.h
@@ -23,7 +23,7 @@
 #include "Soundengine/DSPAudio/FX/Delay.h"
 #include "Soundengine/DSPAudio/FX/Reverb.h"
 
-#define USE_REVERB 0
+#define USE_REVERB 1
 
 enum FxTypeEnum
 {
